.TH START-MU2EDAQ-COMMANDLINE-TOOLS.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.2.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh \- refresh the venv and run mu2edaq\-tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./start\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh
.RB [ \-\-no\-update ]
.RI [ tool\-arguments ...]
.br
.B ./start\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs
.B bootstrap.sh
when
.I venv/
does not exist; otherwise runs it again with its output discarded to refresh
dependencies (this needs network access to the package index).
It then writes its own PID to the pidfile and
.BR exec s
.B venv/bin/python \-m mu2edaq_commandline_tools.cli
with the remaining arguments, so
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./start\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh config \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
is
.B mu2edaq\-tools config \-\-json
inside the venv, without activating it.
.PP
.B bootstrap.sh
is called without
.B \-\-dev
or
.BR \-\-cpp .
.SH OPTIONS
Both options are recognised only as the first argument; anything after them
belongs to
.BR mu2edaq\-tools (1).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-update
Skip the dependency refresh.
Use on nodes without network access.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the script's header comment and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .mu2edaq\-tools.pid
Pidfile in the checkout, unless
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_PIDFILE
is set.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_PIDFILE
Pidfile location.
.PP
All
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_*
configuration variables pass through to the tool; see
.BR mu2edaq\-tools (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of
.BR mu2edaq\-tools ,
or non-zero if
.B bootstrap.sh
fails.
.SH BUGS
The script installs
.B trap 'rm \-f $PIDFILE' EXIT
and then
.BR exec s
Python.
.B exec
replaces the shell, so the trap never runs and the pidfile is left behind
after every invocation, holding a PID that the kernel will eventually reuse.
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh (1)
signals whatever process then holds that PID.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
\&./start\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh otsdaq state \-\-instance crv
\&./start\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh \-\-no\-update config
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-tools (1),
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh (1),
.BR bootstrap.sh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group.
